<title>IRAN: Drought damages 129,000 hectares of grain in Iran.</title>
<headline>Drought damages 129,000 hectares of grain in Iran.</headline>
<dateline>TEHRAN 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>A drought in northeastern Iran has caused extensive damage to wheat and barley crops on 129,000 hectares (320,000 acres) of farmland, the Kayhan evening daily said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The dry spell in Gonbad Kavous province damaged between 20 and 100 percent of crops. Financial damage is estimates at 12.87 billion rials ($4.27 million), the paper said.</p>
<p>Damage to pastures and herds in the area was estimated at another 12 billion rials.</p>
<p>&quot;During the past two months, an unprecedented heat wave has hit Gonbad Kavous, raising the temperature to 38 Celsius (100 Fahrenheit) on some days,&quot; the paper said.</p>
</text>
